        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "CHEBI via OLS (stem-substring)",
          "notes": "Parent class identified via stem-substring; matched_via='ammonium molybdate tetrahydrate'"
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:91249 ('ammonium molybdate') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
          "source": "MIM curation (#312); chebi.db",
          "notes": "identifier cas:12054-85-2 -> CHEBI:86244; ontology CHEBI:91249 ('ammonium molybdate') -> CHEBI:86244 ('hexaammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate'); mapping_quality CLOSE_MATCH -> SYNONYM_MATCH. The record (H32Mo7N6O28, CAS 12054-85-2) is the heptamolybdate; CHEBI:91249 'ammonium molybdate' is the diammonium orthomolybdate (2H4N.MoO4, one Mo), a different polyanion, not the anhydrous parent of this hydrate. ChEBI has the substance: CHEBI:86244 'hexaammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate' (4H2O.6H4N.Mo7O24) carries the related synonym 'ammonium molybdate tetrahydrate', the record's exact label, on no other term. Section 3 step 1 with a unique synonym: SYNONYM_MATCH. The CAS stays on its registry row."
        }
      ]
